 "verdict": "CONTROL: T=0.7 on the binary alphabet reproduces the frozen, non-igniting behaviour already measured. KILL: NO live regime anywhere on the grid -- 18 cells across 3 alphabets and 6 temperatures, none clearing both ignition >= 0.5 and top-share < 0.9. Raising temperature melts the frozen ring but does not buy a spreading regime, so the failure is not the choice of alphabet and not the temperature: it is the RESTRICTION ITSELF. Renormalising a language model's conditional onto a small support removes whatever makes damage spread on the full vocabulary. #105, #106 and #107 close as designed. BOUNDARY: one model, one checkpoint, one radius, and the trajectory is reported per cell so 'never rose' is distinguished from 'rose and died' by inspection. A negative bounds THIS construction, not token-lattice CAs in general.",
